language 0.1.0
module kubernetes
  uses deploy, infrastructure, network, runtime, security, system
  means
    The units Kubernetes places workloads in, addresses them by, configures
    them with and gives storage to — each declared a variety of a standard
    one, and defined in the words of Kubernetes rather than of its
    implementation.

entity cluster : infrastructure:cluster
  means
    cluster: the machines Kubernetes places work upon, together with what
    decides where each piece of work goes.

entity node : infrastructure:host
  means
    node: one machine of a cluster, offering the processor, the memory and
    the storage a workload is placed against.

entity namespace : system:organization
  means
    namespace: a division of a cluster within which names do not repeat and
    against which quotas and rights are set.

entity pod : runtime:process
  means
    pod: the smallest thing Kubernetes places — one or more containers put
    on one node together, sharing an address and a lifetime.

entity container : infrastructure:container
  means
    container: one image running inside a pod, with limits of its own on
    what it may consume.

entity deployment : deploy:deployment
  means
    deployment: a wish for so many alike pods to be running, and the way
    Kubernetes is to move from the pods running now to the pods wished for.

entity service : network:endpoint
  means
    service: one name and one address standing for whichever pods answer to
    a selector at the moment a request arrives.

entity ingress : network:gateway
  means
    ingress: the way a request from outside the cluster reaches a service
    within it, chosen by the host and the path asked for.

entity config-map : deploy:configuration
  means
    config map: settings kept apart from the image, given to a pod as
    variables of its environment or as files.

entity secret : security:asset
  means
    secret: what a workload must have and no reader of the manifests may
    see — a password, a key, a token.

entity persistent-volume : infrastructure:volume
  means
    persistent volume: storage that outlives the pod using it, so that a
    workload may be moved between nodes without losing what it wrote.

entity resource-quota : infrastructure:resource-quota
  means
    resource quota: the ceiling a namespace may consume, counted over
    everything placed within it.
